# Line endings: LF everywhere, in the index AND the working tree, regardless of a machine's
# core.autocrlf. Git for Windows defaults autocrlf=true, which checked out every text file as CRLF —
# that breaks bash on `run-app` and every `*.sh` (`$'\r': command not found`) and puts stray `\r` into
# tests that read source or fixtures and split on "\n". Binary files are still auto-detected.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows-native scripts must stay CRLF; cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only batch files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Vendored third-party text kept byte-for-byte as upstream shipped it (CRLF).
apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources/opsin/OPSIN-LICENSE.txt -text

*.patch whitespace=-blank-at-eol

# Generated model artifacts and audit records. Marked `-diff` so git treats them as opaque: they are
# regenerated by the scripts in `vendor/pka-model/` and by `pkaErrorAudit`, never hand-edited, and a
# line-by-line diff of 22,000 rows of measurement output is noise in every review and every
# `git show`. The FILES still version and still travel; only their textual diff is suppressed.
#
# LISTED INDIVIDUALLY, not globbed. `pka-model/*.json` also swallowed seven small, hand-editable files
# that shipped code imports directly — `calibration.json`, `interval-calibration.json`,
# `hammett-sigma.json`, `edge-variance.json`, `coupling.json`, `consensus-calibration.json` and
# `external-validation.json`, the last being where the headline accuracy claim is read from. A change
# to one of those alters every pKa and every confidence interval the app reports, and it rendered in
# review as `Bin 2031 -> 2044 bytes`. Four files are genuinely too large to read; the rest must stay
# reviewable. `*.npy` is kept as a glob but is also covered by `pka-model/.gitignore`, so it is a
# belt-and-braces entry rather than a live one.
docs/benchmarks/pka-fast-aqueous-error-audit.json -diff
packages/rdkit-adapter/vendor/pka-model/site-pka-forest.json -diff
packages/rdkit-adapter/vendor/pka-model/site-pka-gnn.json -diff
packages/rdkit-adapter/vendor/pka-model/gnn-oof.json -diff
packages/rdkit-adapter/vendor/pka-model/calibration-pairs.json -diff
packages/rdkit-adapter/vendor/pka-model/*.npy -diff
